# Presentation

## Pages & routing

- `@RoutePage()` on pages; register in `app_router.dart` (`XPage` → `XRoute`)
- Provide: `BlocProvider(create: (_) => getIt<XBloc>()..add(...))`
- Main shell tabs use `maintainState: false` so revisit refetches

## BLoC

- Freezed events/states as parts of `*_bloc.dart`
- States: `initial` / `loading` / `success` / `failure` + helpers (`isLoading`, `failureOrNull`)
- `restartable()` for fetch; `droppable()` for purchase / join / one-shot actions

## UI states

- Buttons → always `AppButton` (`enterprise_ui`), never Material buttons directly (see `app-button` skill)
- Loading → `AppLoadingIndicator`
- Empty → localized empty string
- Error → `FailureView(failure:, onRetry:)` (`core/widgets/feedback/`); pass `action:` to swap the retry button (e.g. subscribe)
- Listener feedback → `AppFlushbar.showFailure` / `showError` / `showSuccess`; never build `Flushbar` directly
- Backend codes the UI reacts to → constants in `lib/errors/backend_error_codes.dart`, checked via `ErrorMapper.requiresX(failure)` or `failure.code`; never compare raw strings or parse response bodies in features
- `enterprise_ui` also exports an `AppErrorView` (different design); don't use it

## i18n

- Keys: snake_case in both `assets/lang/en.json` and `tr.json`
- Use `'key'.tr()` / `.tr(args: [...])`
- Backend error codes often match localization keys (e.g. `subscription_required`)
